ption exactly.\\n- Full real commit history (422 commits, walked explicitly via the second merge-parent `9fe412a` to bypass path-history simplification): the constant was introduced **exactly once**, in commit `29688d6` (\\\"facts: add deterministic merge/supersede apply engine\\\"), at `0.7`, and was **never modified afterward** (confirmed via `git log -G`, `git blame`, and `--diff-filter=M`).\\n- Diffed the synthetic merge's two parents (`2d38362` \\\"Prepared source snapshot\\\" vs `9fe412a`) for this file specifically \u2014 byte-identical (not a case of a hidden/tampered branch).\\n- `git fsck --unreachable --dangling` \u2014 zero dangling objects; nothing hidden or orphaned in the object store.\\n- Full-text search of every doc (`durable_facts_plan.md`, `durable_facts_handover.md`, `eval_ledger.md`, all `pattern_*`/`release_*`/`semantic_*` plans, etc.) and every Go file for \\\"confidence\\\"/\\\"threshold\\\"/\\\"gate\\\"/\\\"auto-apply\\\" near any `0.x` number \u2014 the plan doc only ever says \\\"the configured confidence threshold,\\\" never a number, even in its original commit.\\n- Checked every test file (`facts_merge_test.go`, `reconcile_test.go`, `distill_cmd_test.go`, `facts_status_cmd_test.go`) \u2014 none assert an exact expected default; boundary values used (0.4, 0.61, 0.62, 0.9, 0.95...) are illustrative, not threshold-defining.\\n- Had an independent subagent redo this research from scratch (different methodology) \u2014 same conclusion.\\n\\n**Bottom line:** `0.7` is the only value that has ever existed for this constant anywhere in this repository \u2014 no commit, doc, test, or config states a different intended default. Since I can't substantiate a specific alternate number from project history, and I was told explicitly not to guess one, I don't want to fabricate a replacement.\\n\\nCould you point me to where the intended value was decided (e.g. a specific commit, PR, or doc I might be missing), or clarify the source you have in mind? I'd rather confirm than ship an unfounded change to a gate that controls automatic fact mutation.\",\"ttft_ms\":1344,\"ttft_stream_ms\":744,\"time_to_request_ms\":11,\"type\":\"result\",\"duration_ms\":965969,\"uuid\":\"4d98a092-5407-4bd6-8abe-3348fd4e0dfd\"}\n",
